# Box-specific redaction table for ./sync-skills -- TEMPLATE, tracked.
#
# Copy to `.sync-skills.local` (gitignored) and fill in THIS host's names.
# One rule per line:   literal<TAB>placeholder
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: these are plain string replacements applied in sequence,
# so the longest, most specific literal must come first -- a numbered handle
# before its bare stem, a full hostname before the bare domain. A generic pass
# already rewrites any absolute home path to `~`, so a `/home/<user>` rule here is
# only needed when you want the handle ITSELF to stay legible in the output.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT IN THE SCRIPT: the script ships with the repo, and a redaction
# table that spells out a handle, a domain and a box's hostname publishes exactly
# what it was written to remove.
#
# With no `.sync-skills.local`, the script still runs: it redacts and scans for
# generic host-shaped facts (an absolute home path, a private-network address) and
# SAYS that the guard is weaker.
#
# Examples (replace the left column with your own):
# /home/OPERATOR-HOME	~
# OPERATOR-HANDLE	<operator-handle>
# DISPOSABLE-HANDLE	<disposable-handle>
# TEST-HANDLE	<test-handle>
# GPU-BOX-ACCOUNT	<gpu-handle>
# your.public.host	<public-host>
# your-domain.tld	<your-domain>
